    "type": "question",
    "label": "5",
    "prompt": "The sum of two consecutive even numbers is 110. Find the numbers.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$54$ and $56$.",
      "worked": "Let the smaller even number be $x$. Consecutive even numbers differ by $2$, so the larger number is $x+2$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}x+(x+2)&=110\\\\2x+2&=110\\\\2x&=108\\\\x&=54\\end{align*}$$\n\nThe larger number is $54+2=56$.\n\nCheck: $54+56=110$, and $54$ and $56$ are consecutive even numbers.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
